<title>USA: Pathmark Stores Q4 net loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Pathmark Stores Q4 net loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>WOODBRIDGE, N.J. 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>PATHMARK STORES INC.</p>
<p>				(Dollars in Millions)</p>
<p>			     13 Wks  14 Wks	  52 Wks    53 Wks</p>
<p>				Ended   Ended	   Ended     Ended</p>
<p>			     2/1/97  2/3/96	  2/1/97    2/3/96</p>
<p> Sales(a)		 $ 955.3 $1,077.7    $ 3,710.5 $ 3,971.6</p>
<p> Operating earnings   22.7(b)    66.6	127.1(b)     184.5</p>
<p>Gain on disposition</p>
<p>of freestanding</p>
<p>   drug stores		 --	--		--	15.5</p>
<p>Gain on sale of real</p>
<p>   estate			--     3.4		--	 3.4</p>
<p> Interest expense	(40.8)  (41.4)	 (161.4)   (164.7)</p>
<p>Earnings (loss)</p>
<p>   before taxes	  (18.1)    28.6	  (34.3)	38.7</p>
<p>Income tax (provision)</p>
<p>   benefit		    8.1  (10.9)	    14.4  (5.9)(c)</p>
<p>Net earnings (loss)</p>
<p>before extraordinary</p>
<p>   item		    (10.0)    17.7	  (19.9)	32.8</p>
<p>Extraordinary item,</p>
<p>   net of tax benefit(d)   --	--	   (0.9)	  --</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss)   (10.0)    17.7	  (20.8)	32.8</p>
<p>Operating cash flow(e)</p>
<p>				 64.9    86.9	   236.4     268.9</p>
<p>Operating cash flow</p>
<p>   (% of sales)	    6.8%    8.1%	    6.4%	6.8%</p>
<p>Memo:  LIFO charge</p>
<p>   (credit)		 (3.0)   (1.0)	   (1.3)	 1.1</p>
<p>During fiscal 1996, Pathmark changed its reporting of Pathmark coupon expenses from selling, general and administrative expenses to a reduction of sales. Prior periods have been reclassified to conform to the current presentation.</p>
<p>(b) Includes a $9.1 million pretax charge to record reorganization and restructuring costs, including early retirement and severance programs, an $8.8 million pretax charge related to unfavorable lease commitments of certain unprofitable stores held for sale in the company's southern region and a $5.4 million pretax charge to write down certain fixed assets held for sale to their estimated net realizable values.</p>
<p>(c) The fiscal 1995 income tax provision includes a reversal of the deferred income tax valuation allowance of $9.1 million.</p>
<p>(d) Represents loss on early extinguishment of debt.</p>
<p>(e) Operating cash flow represents earnings from operations before interest, income taxes, depreciation, amortization, LIFO charge (credit), restructuring charge and unusual transactions.</p>
